    <div class="blog-body" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); line-height: 1.85; font-size: 1.05rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.08); padding: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid #06b6d4; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;">
            Endlessync is designed as a persistent, boundary-free canvas where actions sync live across all connected participants worldwide. Because every user interacts with the exact same coordinate plane without isolated rooms or locks, understanding how to navigate, manipulate elements, and collaborate smoothly is essential.
        </p>

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                <span>1. Infinite Navigation & Viewport Management</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
                The infinite workspace does not bind you to standard page borders. Instead, you move across a virtual Cartesian coordinate system using panning and zooming.
            </p>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Panning (Moving Across the World)</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Hand / Pan Mode:</strong> Select the Pan tool from the toolbar (or hold down the <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">Spacebar</code>) and click-and-drag anywhere on the canvas.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Trackpad & Mouse:</strong> Two-finger drag on trackpads or clicking and dragging with the middle mouse button allows smooth movement across the board.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Coordinate Awareness:</strong> As you move away from the origin <code>(0, 0)</code>, your viewport dynamically updates to load only the elements within your active field of view to maintain high performance.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Zooming & Scaling</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Mouse Wheel / Pinch-to-Zoom:</strong> Scroll up to zoom in for detailed sketches or text alignment, and scroll down to zoom out for a high-level overview of regional activity.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Minimap & Origin Reset:</strong> If you lose track of your creations in the endless space, use the reset button or minimap control to re-center your viewport back to the origin coordinates <code>(0, 0)</code>.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin: 2rem 0;">

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                <span>2. Real-Time Freehand Drawing & Sketching</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
                The drawing engine broadcasts vector stroke data live, ensuring precision while keeping network bandwidth low.
            </p>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Choosing Tools & Stroke Properties</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Pen Tool:</strong> Activate the brush/pen icon from the main tool rail to begin drawing freehand strokes.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Color Palette:</strong> Select from predefined swatches or open the color picker to change your stroke color.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Stroke Width:</strong> Adjust the slider to switch between fine line annotations (1–3px) and broad markers or graffiti tags (8–20px).</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Eraser & Corrections</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Object vs. Pixel Erasing:</strong> The eraser tool allows you to remove entire stroke paths or target specific lines drawn by you or others.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Undo / Redo:</strong> Use standard shortcuts (<code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #f472b6;">Ctrl+Z</code> / <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #f472b6;">Cmd+Z</code> and <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #f472b6;">Ctrl+Y</code> / <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #f472b6;">Cmd+Shift+Z</code>) for local action history before strokes are committed permanently to the database layer.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin: 2rem 0;">

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                <span>3. Dynamic Text & Thought Placement</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
                Text tools are built for leaving comments, brainstorming, or writing persistent notes directly on the board.
            </p>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Creating Text Blocks</h3>
            <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Click the <strong>Text Tool</strong> (<code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">T</code>) from the toolbar.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Click anywhere on the open canvas where you want your text to anchor.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Type directly into the inline editor.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Formatting & Resizing</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Font Sizing:</strong> Adjust the scale using the contextual floating menu to make header-sized announcements or fine-print annotations.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Color & Alignment:</strong> Align text left, center, or right, and modify font colors to stand out against background doodles or dark sections.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Live Broadcast:</strong> As soon as you complete or commit a text block, it becomes readable in real time to any user viewing that sector of the board.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin: 2rem 0;">

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                <span>4. Image Uploads & Media Placement</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
                Endlessync allows you to anchor external images and graphics onto the shared canvas.
            </p>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Uploading Assets</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>File Upload Button:</strong> Click the media/image icon to select supported image formats (<code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">.png</code>, <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">.jpg</code>, <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">.jpeg</code>, <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">.webp</code>, <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #38bdf8;">.svg</code>) directly from your device.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Drag-and-Drop:</strong> Drag an image file from your desktop directly onto the browser window; the image will automatically place itself at your cursor’s canvas coordinates.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Clipboard Paste:</strong> Copy an image to your clipboard and press <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #f472b6;">Ctrl+V</code> (or <code style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; color: #f472b6;">Cmd+V</code>) while focusing on the board to drop it instantly into the view.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Transforming Images</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Moving:</strong> Click and drag the image across the board to re-position it.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Rescaling:</strong> Select an image to activate bounding corner anchors. Drag any corner handle inward or outward to scale the graphic while maintaining aspect ratio.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Layering & Overlap:</strong> Images act as layered objects, allowing other users to sketch notes over them or frame them with drawings.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin: 2rem 0;">

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                <span>5. Global Real-Time Collaboration & Etiquette</span>
            </h2>
            <p>
                Because Endlessync is completely open with no private rooms, passwords, or locks, the board is an ever-shifting public mural.
            </p>
            <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Live Presence:</strong> When other participants are working within your visible screen area, updates appear instantly as they are committed.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Collaborative Layering:</strong> You can expand on existing ideas by adding notes adjacent to other sketches, building collective mind maps, or answering questions left by users on different continents.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Shared Space Etiquette:</strong> Remember that anyone can pan to your location, read your notes, or modify nearby space. Avoid placing oversized images over smaller collaborative sketches, and treat the canvas as a continuously evolving public commons.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
